- How would you extend to support field renames without changing consumer code?
- How would you test compatibility across v1 and v2 payloads in a canary run?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests per-key stateful processing, TTL-based windowing, and idempotence across replays—core KCNA concepts—while exercising cross-event aggregation and emission semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key in-memory or stateful session store with a 30-second TTL
- Idempotent emits using a deterministic sessionId (userId:start)
- Out-of-order arrivals handled via lastEventTs and session boundaries
- At-least-once delivery guaranteed by committing offsets only after emit

## Code Example
```javascript
function onMessage(ctx, msg) {
  const session = sessionStore().getOrCreate(msg.userId, () => ({
    startTs: msg.timestamp,
    endTs: msg.timestamp,
    count: 0,
    lastEventTs: msg.timestamp
  }));
  session.endTs = msg.timestamp;
  session.lastEventTs = msg.timestamp;
  session.count++;
  sessionStore().setTtl(msg.userId, 30000, () => {
    ctx.emit('sessions', {
      userId: msg.userId,
      sessionStart: session.startTs,
      sessionEnd: session.endTs,
      eventCount: session.count
    });
    sessionStore().remove(msg.userId);
  });
}

function commitOffsets() {
  ctx.commit();
}

function sessionStore() {
  return ctx.state();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Privacy-first multi-tenant KCNA is a real challenge; rotation and audit are painful at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption
- Per-tenant KMS keys
- On-the-fly rotation with no downtime
- Audit trails and access control
- Backward compatibility with legacy envelopes
- Canary tests for rotation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: envelope encrypt data per tenant
function encryptForTenant(tenantId, plaintext, version) {
  const keyId = kms.getKeyId(tenantId, version);
  const dataKey = kms.generateDataKey(tenantId, version);
  const ciphertext = crypto.aesGcmEncrypt(dataKey.plaintext, plaintext);
  const envelope = { keyId, cipher: ciphertext, iv: dataKey.iv };
  return envelope;
}
```

